{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals","id":1281384,"title":"Using Mind to possess animals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-17T15:24:22-08:00","id":1281384,"title":"Using Mind to possess animals","content":"Question #1: What level of Mind do I need to possess an animal, such that I control it's every action, and perceive the world through its senses? I think it's probably <b>Mind 4</b>.<br /> <br /> Question #2: If I &quot;multi-task&quot; with Mind 1, can I use one of those mental actions to control the animal as before, such that I would walk around going about my day, while also controlling and perceiving through the animal?<br /> <br /> At any rate, please let me know what spheres would actually be necessary to accomplish these feats. I think, at most, it would be Mind 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T04:27:00-08:00","id":1281483,"title":"","content":"Question 1: Mind 4 could be possible, but Correspondence would also be necessary. You'd have to basically transpose your conciosness over the animal, therefore a spacial/relation component is needed.<br /> <br /> Question 2: I'd rule this only possible if you co-locate your consciosnes. So, it's another Mind/Correspondence spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T06:47:48-08:00","id":1281500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals?p=1281483#post1281483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question 1: Mind 4 could be possible, but Correspondence would also be necessary. You'd have to basically transpose your conciosness over the animal, therefore a spacial/relation component is needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that, since Astral Travel allows your mind to leave your body and travel anywhere w/o Correspondence, you can possess an animal to control it w/o Correspondence at Mind 4-5...if you're willing to leave your body and invade the animal's mind, that is. Using Mind 4 this way it's less effective than Mind 5 because it only allows to travel out of body for a few minutes<br /> <br /> Otherwise, yes, you would need Corr 4 to control the animal at distance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-18-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T07:59:14-08:00","id":1281510,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd rule you would need time 3, Corr 3.<br /> <br /> Just colocating your consciousness doesn't allow you to act additional times. So instead you'd be speeding your mind up so that you could take two mental actions, thereby commanding two bodies. Correspondence is just for linkage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T11:04:09-08:00","id":1281535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals?p=1281510#post1281510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I'd rule you would need time 3, Corr 3.<br /> <br /> Just colocating your consciousness doesn't allow you to act additional times. So instead you'd be speeding your mind up so that you could take two mental actions, thereby commanding two bodies. Correspondence is just for linkage.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can't I use Mind 1 to allow me to multi-task (i.e., take additional mental actions each turn)? And if that's the case, couldn't I use one of my &quot;multi-task mind turns&quot; to control the animal from one moment to the next?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T11:32:06-08:00","id":1281540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals?p=1281535#post1281535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can't I use Mind 1 to allow me to multi-task (i.e., take additional mental actions each turn)? And if that's the case, couldn't I use one of my &quot;multi-task mind turns&quot; to control the animal from one moment to the next?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes you can gain multi-tasking trough MInd 1. But what that means it's not necessarily clear. In Revised at least it wasn't clear, perhaps in M20 it is clear, I don't remember.<br /> <br /> It could mean that you get a difficulty reduction or something like that when doing more than one mental task at the same time. A bit like being &quot;ambidextrous&quot; in Mage (as per the Merit) doesn't really grant you one extra action. I don't think &quot;multi-task&quot; explicitly states that these extra actions are completely w/o penalty.<br /> <br /> I think that would take either Time 3 (as Enginseer-42 says) or co-location (independant bodies created trough Correspondendce, Life and Mind can act independantly w/o penalty, and thus independant minds can think independantly for the same reason)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-18-2019, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T13:00:31-08:00","id":1281552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals?p=1281540#post1281540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could mean that you get a difficulty reduction or something like that when doing more than one mental task at the same time. A bit like being &quot;ambidextrous&quot; in Mage (as per the Merit) doesn't really grant you one extra action. I don't think &quot;multi-task&quot; explicitly states that these extra actions are completely w/o penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Revised really <i><b>is </b></i>quite vague; it says under the entry for Mind 1: &quot;[T]he initiate . . . can perform a number of prodigious, but usually coincidental, mental feats.&quot; M:tAs(Rev.), 175. Under the common effect of <i>Mind Empowerment</i>:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> She can focus on multiple tasks at once . . . . [e]mpowering mental processes allows the make to function like a calculator or computer. . . . [t]he successes scored . . . allow the mage to multi-task and concentrate on multiple avenues of thought at once. Although the mage still moves, responds, and acts at his normal rate, he can engage in battle while simultaneously thinking about several problems and deciding what sort of tie to wear to a formal dinner later that evening.<br /> <br /> M:tAs(Rev.), 176. </div> </div> </div>Systematically, I think this implies that you get an extra 'mental task' for every success spent towards that purpose; e.g., four successes grants for extra mental tasks that can be performed per turn (subject to whatever the duration of the effect happens to be). Certainly you could construe this as having to do with penalties or something, but my reading of this seems to be that, normally, one simply <i>cannot</i> perform more than one mental task at a time, penalty or not.<br /> <br /> That said, the Revised version of the Ambidextrous merits is crazy overpowered, and is unique in its construction, not only across editions, but <i>games</i>. In essence, it gives you a free action:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your mage has equal facility with either hand. You never suffer a penalty for your character\u2019s use of either hand in performing a task, since the character has no \u201coff-hand.\u201d <b>The character can use both hands at once to perform two physical tasks without splitting dice pools</b>, but he may suffer a concentration penalty ( at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion), especially if the tasks are wildly different or in different arcs of vision. Very few people are truly ambidextrous. In stressful situations, a penalty should always be assessed for the difficulty of performing actions with both hands at once.<br /> <br /> M:tAs(Rev.), 288. (emphasis added) </div> </div> </div>To be fair the game goes out of its way to stay there could be a concentration penalty depending upon the circumstances, but I would argue that this is greatly mitigated to the extent that someone is (a) out of combat or otherwise not engaged in some life-or-death task; (b) has the &quot;Concentration&quot; merit; (c) has a Mind 1 effect on themselves to improve concentration (possibly by buying down whatever penalty); or some combination of these. This is a conversation for another day, but it certainly seems like if a character is holding a gun in each hand and is firing at the same target, that they'd be able to fire both guns without splitting their dice pool. A ST might, as a matter of overriding policy, simply not allow that for game balance reasons, but as written the merit would seem to support this operation of the merit.<br /> <br /> I digress, everyone knows there is some truly wild shit in Revised. M20 says only this: &quot;On a related note, he also learns how to multitask and absorb data with startling acuity. Each success he rolls allows him to either consider an additional subject or speed the processing time that a normal person might require.&quot; M20, 519. My read on this version is that it's a greatly curtailed version of &quot;multitasking&quot;. I don't know how much you want to read into the lack of a comma between the word &quot;multitask&quot; and the words &quot;and absorb data&quot;, but to the extent that the people who wrote the book are users of the oxford comma, and the omission of a comma there is significant (i.e., &quot;multitask&quot; is further defined by &quot;absorb data&quot;, rather than these being two separate things than can both be accomplished independent of one another) I would say the multitask effect is probably strictly limited to feats of analysis and/or introspection.<br /> <br /> My broad interpretation, as a storyteller, of the ability to multi-task is that it refers to taking more than one mental action, not including casting magic; or, put more 'oomph' into a single mental process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals?p=1281540#post1281540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I think that would take either Time 3 (as Enginseer-42 says) or co-location (independant bodies created trough Correspondendce, Life and Mind can act independantly w/o penalty, and thus independant minds can think independantly for the same reason)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ultimately, I find everyone's explanation over the need for Correspondence <u><i>highly</i></u> persuasive. Time, less so, for reasons that should be obvious given my discussion above about how I construe the mechanical operation of what it means to be able to multi-task with one's mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":2319,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","user":"CaptOtter","date":". 01-18-2019, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T13:53:32-08:00","id":1281568,"title":"","content":"Edit: missed the muti-tasking aspect. Never mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-18-2019, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T05:11:53-08:00","id":1281928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My broad interpretation, as a storyteller, of the ability to multi-task is that it refers to taking more than one mental action, not including casting magic; or, put more 'oomph' into a single mental process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it's certainly possible. I think it's a reasonable interpretation and Mind IT'S a Sphere that's known for allowing to do extraordinary things at lower levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-10T18:45:11-07:00","id":1443433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals#post1281384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question #1: What level of Mind do I need to possess an animal, such that I control it's every action, and perceive the world through its senses? I think it's probably <b>Mind 4</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shouldn't this depend on the complexity of the animal mind? If you're possessing an insect to scout some hard to get into place it should be less than that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2078-alucard","name":"Alucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2078_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"811"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T21:21:45-07:00","id":1443560,"title":"","content":"There is a rote that does this in Dead Magic 2, using only Mind 4. But it is based specifically on Norse seidr workings, that of ritually chanting one's self into a trance and sending your soul out and about in the world, with possession of an animal being one of the things your soul can do. This is based off of Astral Projection and Possession being among the stuff Mind 4 has always been able to do, IIRC, as well as the fact that the user is unaware of what is going on at her body while projecting. Different cultures/styles may tackle the problem differently. <br /> <br /> Hmm. Ethernetic Mind Control Helmets ... \ud83e\udd14","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T11:53:33-07:00","id":1443774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1281384-using-mind-to-possess-animals?p=1443560#post1443560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. Ethernetic Mind Control Helmets ... \ud83e\udd14</div> </div> </div> </div> I can see that. Like the Mad Hatter from Batman. Come to think of it, a Hat-like control device that controls people whose head is in physical contact with a playing card-sized object isn't bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}